## Context

## Contexto

O CI atual roda \`vitest\` mas não impõe nenhum threshold de cobertura — é possível adicionar código sem testes e o pipeline passa.

## Proposta

Configurar thresholds no \`vitest.config.ts\`:

\`\`\`typescript
// vitest.config.ts
export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    coverage: {
      provider: 'v8',
      thresholds: {
        lines: 90,
        functions: 90,
        branches: 85,
        statements: 90,
      },
      include: ['src/**'],
      exclude: ['src/index.ts'], // barrel sem lógica
    },
  },
});
\`\`\`

E adicionar o step no CI:

\`\`\`yaml
- name: Test with coverage
  run: npm run test:coverage
\`\`\`

> **Nota:** os thresholds só fazem sentido depois que as issues #3 e #4 (testes faltando) forem resolvidas — do contrário o pipeline falhará imediatamente.

## Critério de aceitação

- \`npm run test:coverage\` falha se cobertura cair abaixo do threshold
- CI falha em PRs que removem cobertura

The app blocked all functionality when served from any non-loopback hostname, making it impossible to deploy remotely. The server was already deployment-ready (binds all interfaces, respects `process.env.PORT`, relative API paths) — the only blocker was a client-side guard.

## Changes

- **`index.html`**: Removed `isLocalServer()`, `NOT_LOCAL_MSG`, and the two guard checks that short-circuited `fetchInfo()` and `startDownload()` for non-localhost origins

```js
// Before — blocked on any remote host
async function fetchInfo() {
  if (!isLocalServer()) return showStatus(NOT_LOCAL_MSG, 'error');
  ...
}

// After — works on any host
async function fetchInfo() {
  ...
}
```

