`@analytics` and `@reports` slot directories lived under the `(dashboard)/` route group — a segment with no `layout.tsx` — so Next.js never delivered them to any parent. `StatCards` and `AccountAuditComponent` were exported but never rendered.

## Changes

### Slot relocation
- `git mv` both `@analytics/` and `@reports/` from `(dashboard)/` → `(dashboard)/dashboard/`, the segment whose `layout.tsx` actually exists

### Slot implementation (×2 slots)
- **`page.tsx`** — renders the component at the `/dashboard` root
- **`default.tsx`** — returns `null` on all sub-routes (`/dashboard/account/…`); without this Next.js 404s the entire page on hard navigation
- **`loading.tsx`** — independent Suspense skeleton per slot; a slow audit query no longer blocks stat cards from streaming

### Layout update
```tsx
// dashboard/layout.tsx
export default function DashboardLayout({
  children, header, modal,
  analytics, // ← new
  reports,   // ← new
}: DashboardLayoutProps) {
  return (
    <SidebarInset>
      {header}
      <ThemeAdapter>
        <main className="flex-1 space-y-8 overflow-y-auto p-6">
          {analytics}
          {children}
          {reports}
        </main>
      </ThemeAdapter>
      {modal}
    </SidebarInset>
  );
}
```

